# Histogram & Skewness 📊

## 📌 Introduction
A histogram and skewness are important concepts in Statistics and Data Analytics. A histogram represents the distribution of numerical data using bars, while skewness helps us understand the shape and asymmetry of the distribution.

This folder contains Python practice examples to understand data distribution and identify whether data is symmetric or skewed.

## 🎯 Objectives
- Understand histograms and their uses.
- Visualize numerical data distributions.
- Learn positive, negative, and zero skewness.
- Understand how the mean and median relate to skewness.
- Practice statistical analysis using Python.

